# chat: `hi` is answered by the code model (the `--mock` agent trajectory's one prose-only reply turn) — a [you] bubble, a
# [jevcode] reply, no card, no run chrome: under the agent default (AGENT-LOOP-DESIGN §A1) the greeting IS an agent run that
# stops `answered` and renders as a reply only (run-smoke.sh `answered_reply`). The badge is the default (`agent`) and the
# wall time Enter → [jevcode] is read from the timing file (§8.2 chat-hi)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
sleep 0.2
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
mark hi-sent
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*hi
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* Hi
mark hi-reply
expect agent
expect Follow-up
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
